{"method":"item/completed","params":{"item":{"type":"dynamicToolCall","id":"H1-model-002","namespace":null,"tool":"instruction_read","arguments":{"resource_id":"content-public","spans":null},"status":"completed","contentItems":[{"type":"inputText","text":"<instruction>\n---\nname: sg-content\ndescription: Public documentation and audience-content lifecycles.\n---\n\n# sg-content\n\n## Mission\n\n`sg-content` is the public owner for editorial brand expression, public documentation, and audience content.\n\n## Scope Gate\n\nResolve the product, audience, and public surface, then load `$SHIPGLOWS_ROOT/skills/references/intent-to-outcome-autonomy.md`. Own the public-content outcome from source and claims through validation and publication readiness.\n\n## Required References\n\nResolve `$SHIPGLOWS_ROOT` through the shared canonical-path doctrine, verify the root and `$SHIPGLOWS_ROOT/skills/007-sg-content/SKILL.md` exist, then load that canonical engine for the detailed content lifecycle. If the root or file is missing, stop with a visible error; never fall back to a sibling runtime path. Keep internal editorial engines invisible to the operator; `007-sg-content` is expert/legacy only.\n\n## Validation\n\nUse the selected lifecycle's source, claim, audience-fit, and publication-readiness proof.\n\n## Stop Conditions\n\nStop and follow the runtime contract when the audience, claims, publication authority, or required proof is unresolved.\n\n## Report Modes\n\nLoad `$SHIPGLOWS_ROOT/skills/references/reporting-contract.md` before reporting; keep internal engine names out of user-facing reports.\n\n</instruction>"}],"success":true,"durationMs":144},"threadId":"01a11cde-9f17-7a82-851d-bc77c01cd35c","turnId":"01a11cde-a1c9-7643-9dfd-251d18f30673","completedAtMs":1791485715467},"emittedAtMs":1791485715467}
